    "answer": {
      "short": "\\$800 to \\$400 is a decrease of 50%.",
      "worked": "\\$400 is half of \\$800, so the decrease multiplier is $0.5$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Percentage decrease}&=(1-0.5)\\times100\\%\\\\\\text{Percentage decrease}&=50\\%\\end{align*}$$\nThe increase of 100% is correct. The return decrease is measured from \\$800; a 100% decrease would leave \\$0.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
